@page "/"
@inject IConfiguration Configuration

<PageTitle>SSE Authentication Demos</PageTitle>

<div class="page-shell">
    <h1>SSE Authentication Demos</h1>
    <p>
        This project demonstrates five ways to authenticate Server-Sent Events (SSE) connections.
        Start by logging in if you want to run the token-based demos, then open each dedicated page: 
        <p>Username: demo_user</p>
        <p>Password: test</p>
    </p>

    <h2>How to test</h2>
    <ol>
        <li>Run the Aspire app host so Keycloak, API, and web app are available.</li>
        <li>Use the login button in the top navigation for token-based demos.</li>
        <li>Open one demo page at a time and click <strong>Start</strong>.</li>
        <li>Confirm the counter increments every second.</li>
    </ol>

    <div class="panel-grid">
        <article class="endpoint-panel">
            <h3>1) Cookies - Same-Origin</h3>
            <p>Runs from the API origin so the page and SSE endpoint share the same origin.</p>
            <p><a href="@SameOriginDemoUrl" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open same-origin cookie demo</a></p>
        </article>
        <article class="endpoint-panel">
            <h3>2) Cookies - Cross-Origin</h3>
            <p>Uses credentialed cross-origin EventSource from the Blazor app to the API.</p>
            <p><a href="/demo/cookies-cross-origin">Open cross-origin cookie demo</a></p>
        </article>
        <article class="endpoint-panel">
            <h3>3) Short-Lived Token</h3>
            <p>Fetches a short-lived token first, then sends it as a query parameter on SSE connect.</p>
            <p><a href="/demo/short-lived-token">Open short-lived token demo</a></p>
        </article>
        <article class="endpoint-panel">
            <h3>4) microsoft/fetch-event-source</h3>
            <p>Uses the fetch-event-source library and includes Bearer token authentication in headers.</p>
            <p><a href="/demo/fetch-event-source">Open fetch-event-source demo</a></p>
        </article>
        <article class="endpoint-panel">
            <h3>5) HTTP Client (DotNetSseClient)</h3>
            <p>Uses DotNetSseClient with a bearer token provider configured in DI.</p>
            <p><a href="/demo/http-client">Open HTTP client demo</a></p>
        </article>
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    private string SameOriginDemoUrl => $"{Configuration["ApiUrl"]}/cookie-same-origin-demo.html";
}